<para id="X39400000R702AC" category="C" type-id="3008S" name-id="066NQ-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>P0171/25</dtccode>
<dtcname>Lean Malfunction (Bank1)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0172/26</dtccode>
<dtcname>Rich Malfunction (Bank1)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0174/25</dtccode>
<dtcname>Lean Malfunction (Bank2)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0175/26</dtccode>
<dtcname>Rich Malfunction (Bank2)</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000R702AC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000FOP00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>Detected when the fuel correction amount by the upstream air fuel ratio sensor exceeds a specified value.</ptxt>
<ptxt>There are 2 types of air-fuel ratio correction: normal operation air-fuel ratio correction (hereafter referred to as F/B correction) and operating condition memory air-fuel ratio correction (hereafter referred to as F/B learning).</ptxt>
<ptxt>F/B correction is fuel correction used to maintain the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio. The engine control computer receives the signal from the air fuel ratio sensor indicating whether the current air-fuel ratio is richer (hereafter referred to as rich) or leaner (hereafter referred to as lean) than the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio, and decreases the injection volume if rich or increases it if lean.</ptxt>
<ptxt>F/B learning is control that, when F/B correction has been performed for a certain period of time, adapts to individual engine differences (caused by aging, changes in operating environment, etc.) to bring F/B correction close to zero.</ptxt>
<ptxt>If the condition in which the fuel correction amount (total of F/B correction value and F/B learning value) exceeds a certain value and becomes lean or rich continues for 2 consecutive trips, the engine control computer illuminates the check engine warning light.</ptxt>
<ptxt>Also, when the vehicle runs out of fuel, the fuel correction amount becomes +35% or more, and if this continues (2 trips), lean malfunction P0171/25 or P0174/25 may be output.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
