<step1>
<ptxt>Check of the change pattern of the fuel correction amount (total of F/B correction amount and F/B learning value)</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>If the check engine light illuminated during idling and racing (approx. 2500 r/min) or while driving, reproduce the engine load in the freeze frame data by driving or engine stall, etc., check the fuel correction amount data using SST (TaSCAN), and analyze the malfunction.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A159693J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.76in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Point</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Pattern A (Air Suction)</ptxt>
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>With air suction, the fuel correction amount is large at idle and decreases when racing the engine. This is because the required intake air volume increases when racing, so the proportion of the air suction malfunction relatively decreases</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Intake System</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Pattern B (Intake Air Flow Meter Sub-assembly Malfunction or Injector Clogging)</ptxt>
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The fuel correction amount is very large at both idle and racing; intake air flow meter sub-assembly malfunction and injector clogging show very similar tendencies.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Intake Air Flow Meter Sub-assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Injector</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Pattern C (Intake Air Flow Meter Sub-assembly Malfunction)</ptxt>
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The fuel correction amount increases greatly when racing compared to idle.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>This occurs because the characteristic deviation differs from the intake air flow meter sub-assembly malfunction of pattern B.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Intake Air Flow Meter Sub-assembly</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>After checking the change pattern data, when confirming the vehicle problem symptom under the malfunction condition, use the methods in steps 4 and 5.</ptxt>
</step2>
</step1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000R702AC_12" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000FOQ00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the Freeze Frame Data. Part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred is recorded as freeze frame data, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After repairing or replacing the malfunctioning part, use SST (TaSCAN) to inspect whether [ECU Data Monitor] - [F/B Correction Value Bank 1] and [F/B Learning Value Bank 1] are normal.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>Standard:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Item Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Total of [F/B Correction Bank 1] and [F/B Learning Value Bank 1]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Vehicle condition when malfunction occurred (idling, road test, etc.)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Within ±20 %</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the malfunction occurred during high-speed driving, measurement is possible at medium or low speed by shifting down and matching the intake air volume to that when the malfunction occurred.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000R702AC_14" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000R702AC_14_0088" proc-id="RM0550J___0000FP100000">
<testtitle>Customer Problem Analysis</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>For the customer problem analysis check sheet, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QR01HD"/></ptxt>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000R702AC_14_0048" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000R702AC_14_0048" proc-id="RM0550J___0000FOR00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, display the [Diagnosis Function Menu] - [Mode Change] screen and select check mode. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the screen display of SST (TaSCAN), check the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>If DTCs for an open or short in the sensor circuits are output, perform the related troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.06in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P0171/25, P0172/26, P0174/25 and P0175/26 output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Codes other than P0171/25, P0172/26, P0174/25, P0175/26 are output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000R702AC_14_0089" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="X39400000R702AC_14_0074" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000R702AC_14_0089" proc-id="RM0550J___0000FP200000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Fuel Injection Volume)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the fuel injection volume is increased or decreased, the air fuel ratio sensor output changes. (For a lean malfunction, change the injection volume toward the increase side; for a rich malfunction, toward the decrease side)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>For a lean malfunction, the mixture becomes temporarily rich when racing.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the F/B status on SST (TaSCAN) is "Operating 1", the air fuel ratio sensor is judged to be normal.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Start the engine.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Fuel Injection Volume].</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>System selection screen: Powertrain → TCCS → Active Test</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
