<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Intake Air Amount Inspection</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Inspect indoors with the vehicle level and the engine stopped.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Perform the inspection with the intake air flow meter sub-assembly installed to the air cleaner case (installed on the vehicle).</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Do not extract exhaust from the exhaust tail pipe with an exhaust duct.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and wait for 30 seconds. (Engine stopped)</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [ECU Data Monitor] - [Intake Air Volume] and read the intake air volume.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>0.5 g/s or less</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Sensor Foreign Matter Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A154164J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Visually check the platinum filament (heater) in the flow passage.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Criteria</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No visible foreign matter</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If there is no foreign matter, reinstall the air flow meter to the vehicle after checking.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000R702AC_14_0057" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000R702AC_14_0079" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
